# ── build output and local junk ────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
**/src-tauri/target/
target/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.env
.env.*
*.local

# ── the lab bench: rebuilt, never committed ────────────────────────────────
# raw/ holds every corpus document and every stripped/intermediate output of
# every round. It is reconstructed from committed manifests:
#   node build-corpus.mjs · build-oos.mjs · build-round4..7.mjs · build-pureoos.mjs
# out/ is generated (graph.json, synergy.html, eval.json) by graph.mjs / pipeline.mjs.
raw/
out/

# ── Singapore judgments: published by the courts, NOT redistributable ──────
# Owner ruling 2026-07-23, matching simpler-red: eLitigation text may not be
# republished. Manifests carry the URLs so anyone can refetch; our own
# annotations are a separate question (see REDACTION_AUDIT.md).
# raw/ already covers the corpus copies; these catch strays outside it.
**/sg-judgment-*.txt
**/sg-r[0-9]-*.txt
**/sghcf-r[0-9]-*.txt
**/*.elitigation.htm

# ── the gold: offsets ship, span text does not ─────────────────────────────
# See WITHHELD.md and the header of gold-offsets.mjs. pii-bench/*-offsets/ IS
# committed — it is the published ground truth. What must never be committed is
# anything holding the span text itself: the hydrated tree a user builds from
# their own corpus copy, and the SGHCF annotations, which are withheld outright
# because they index where a court's own party-anonymisation failed.
pii-bench/withheld/
raw/gold-hydrated/

# ── model weights and vendored binaries ────────────────────────────────────
# The E2B is hash-pinned and located at runtime (MODEL_DISCOVERY.md); it is
# never a repo asset. Same for the llama.cpp build and OCR language data.
*.gguf
*.bin
!app/extract/**/*.bin
llama-cuda/
*.traineddata
*.zip
# the Node runtime the packaged app ships as a Tauri sidecar (tauri.conf.json
# bundle.externalBin): a build input placed on the machine, never a repo asset
app/src-tauri/binaries/

# ── run scratch: per-session outputs of the serving adapter ────────────────
_serve/
**/_*.log
**/_*.err

# ── local working notes, not part of the record ───────────────────────────
/1a.txt
/TASKS_OVERNIGHT.md
/MORNING.md

# Agent-run scratch: the argument payload handed to a multi-agent audit. It is
# derived data — every field in it is recomputed by facets.mjs from corpus/ —
# and it is keyed to one run, so it is a session artifact rather than a receipt.
/.wf-args.json

# The opinion text the viewer's "Read the opinion" fetches. These are byte copies
# of corpus/ and newcases/, which are already tracked — generated by
# sync-viewer.mjs, which app/frontend's predev/prebuild run. Tracking them would
# put a second copy of 1.5MB of the same public-domain opinions in the history.
app/frontend/public/cases/
